data.content:
## What Changed

Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0 upgrades to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets OpenAPI 3.1. This is a major breaking change:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` types (`OpenApiString`, etc.) | `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Nullable` property | Type array includes `"null"` |
| `schema.Example` (`IOpenApiAny`) | `schema.Example` (`JsonNode`) |
| `OpenApiSecurityScheme` with `Reference` | `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference` |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` | `Dictionary<OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference, IList<string>>` |
| `operation.Responses.TryAdd(key, OpenApiResponse)` | Same pattern but `OpenApiResponse.Description` → check constructor |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // IOpenApiAny → JsonNode
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // OpenApiSecurityScheme + Reference → OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference
    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // schema.Nullable removed in OpenAPI 3.1;
                // instead, add "null" to the type array or remove it
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of Fixes

1. **`new OpenApiString("1.0")`** → `JsonValue.Create("1.0")` — remove `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any`, use `System.Text.Json.Nodes`
2. **`OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = ... }`** → `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2")` — from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References`
3. **`property.Value.Nullable = false`** → remove the `Null` flag from `property.Value.Type` using the `JsonSchemaType` flags enum
